 61NI c  ABST$The {+61}Ni nuclide has been updated from its previous version    
 61NI2c  published in 2015Zu01, Nuclear Data Sheets. This update was prompted   
 61NI3c  by an enquiry from a user through the IAEA-Nuclear Data Sheets about   
 61NI4c  the absolute intensities of |g rays from {+61}Cu |e decay, as this     
 61NI5c  isotope is important in medical applications and nuclear reaction      
 61NI6c  cross section determinations. This decay has been re-evaluated with    
 61NI7c  the consideration of all the published |g-ray data obtained using Ge   
 61NI8c  detectors. The Q values and particle-separation energies have been     
 61NI9c  revised from 2017Wa10. New references added: 2019Sa04 for a new        
 61NIAc  ({+7}Li,|an|g) reaction dataset; 2019Gy04 and 2015Cv01 for the         
 61NIBc  half-life of {+61}Cu decay; 2018MuZY for neutron resonances; 2016Mo15  
 61NICc  for one-neutron pickup channel reaction, and 2016St14 for evaluated    
 61NIDc  quadrupole moment. The Adopted dataset has been revised and updated    
 61NIEc  according to the modifications made in the individual datasets.        
 61NI c  CUT$Literature available up to January 20, 2020 has been considered.   
 61NI c  ACKN$                                                                  
